Always follow these standards for ALL Playwright API test files:

STRUCTURE:
- Every test file must use test.describe() to group related tests
- Every test file must have these hooks where applicable:
  test.beforeAll()  → login once, get tokens, setup shared data
  test.afterAll()   → cleanup created resources, logout/invalidate tokens
  test.beforeEach() → reset request context, log test name starting
  test.afterEach()  → log test result, attach response to Allure report

DATA DRIVEN:
- ALL test payloads live in test-data/*.json — never hardcoded in spec files
- Each JSON file has sections: valid, invalid, boundary, edge_cases
- Loop over invalid/boundary datasets using test.each() or forEach

ALLURE REPORTING:
- Every test must have:
  allure.epic()     → module name (Auth, Student, Faculty etc)
  allure.feature()  → feature name (Login, Register, Proposal etc)
  allure.story()    → specific scenario
  allure.severity() → critical / normal / minor
  allure.step()     → wrap every action block in a named step
- Attach request payload and response body to every test as Allure attachment
- Attach status code as Allure parameter

CODE QUALITY:
- No hardcoded URLs — always use baseURL from config
- No hardcoded credentials — always from .env via process.env
- No magic numbers — use named constants for status codes
- Every test is independent — no test depends on state from another
- All spec files must have a JSDoc comment block at the top explaining 
  what module is being tested and what is covered
